      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Talladega was incorporated in 1835 and serves as the county seat of Talladega County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talladega%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Talladega Superspeedway, home to NASCAR’s most famous races, draws speed fans from across the nation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/talladega/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The First National Bank of Talladega, founded in 1848, is Alabama’s oldest bank still operating today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talladega%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Creek Indians first settled the area; Andrew Jackson defeated them there in 1813, forcing their departure in the 1830s.",
